commercial revenue or commercial advantage.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

* selling the Work;
* selling a Modified Work;
* bundling the Work into a paid product;
* charging users for access to software containing the Work;
* using the Work as part of a paid service;
* using the Work in a commercial hosting service;
* using the Work in a monetized Minecraft server;
* using the Work in a server or service generating revenue;
* charging subscription fees for a service based upon the Work;
* using the Work to provide paid functionality to customers;
* using the Work as part of a commercial SaaS or hosted service;
* advertising-supported deployment where the Work materially contributes to
  the commercial service;
* sponsorship-supported commercial deployment;
* using the Work for paid consulting, implementation, or service delivery;
* using the Work internally for a commercial organization's business
  operations where the Work materially contributes to commercial activity;
* distributing the Work or a Modified Work for commercial advantage; and
* any substantially similar activity whose primary purpose or effect is
  commercial exploitation.

Commercial Use does not require that money be paid directly for the Work.

A use may constitute Commercial Use even where the Work itself is provided
free of charge.

### 2.8 "Non-Commercial Use"

"Non-Commercial Use" means use that is not intended or reasonably expected
to generate commercial revenue or commercial advantage.

Examples may include:

* personal experimentation;
* personal Minecraft servers;
* educational projects;
* academic research;
* classroom use;
* hobby projects;
* non-profit projects;
* private testing;
* demonstrations;
* personal development;
* public discussion;
* code study; and
* non-commercial modifications and forks.

A person's use of the Work being free of charge does not automatically make
the use Non-Commercial.

### 2.9 "Commercial Authorization"

"Commercial Authorization" means explicit written permission granted by the
Licensor or an authorized representative of the Neko-Nikki Organization
